{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4712",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which are involved in the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone), a key component of the electron transport chain. This suggests that Metformin may influence the function of Nadh Dehydrogenase through these targets. The evidence indicates that Ndufb6, a subunit of Nadh Dehydrogenase, is a downstream participant in this metabolic pathway, implying a potential role for Metformin in modulating Ndufb6 activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, with Metformin potentially affecting the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase through its interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, which in turn influence Ndufb6. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Metformin could exert its effects on cellular metabolism, particularly in relation to mitochondrial function.",
